Description: core: stereo3d_unpack puts a 2D picture in both eyes
 packing=mono: a 2D picture of a 3D project (a 2D clip, a title, a still, a
 colour) is the same picture for both eyes, at the screen plane. As the first
 filter of a producer the filter fits the picture, keeping its shape, into each
 half of the frame, with transparency around it, as MLT pads any picture
 smaller than its frame; the picture's own alpha is kept, so a title over a 3D
 clip lets the clip's pair show under it. A picture the producer makes (a
 colour, a title) has one eye's size, never the frame's. In a producer the
 filter asks for the producer's own picture with the rescale size a filter
 after it suggested cleared (qimage and kdenlivetitle take that suggestion
 over the size asked), and clears the frame's alpha mask once the
 transparency is in the picture. eye_request=1 asks a frame sequence for one
 eye's size in a frame of two eyes.
